WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.070
Hi, everyone.

2
00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:07.610
We recorded today's episode a few weeks ago, but before we play it for you today,

3
00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:14.350
we wanted to pop on because Jenna, you shared something very personal on your Instagram,

4
00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:18.010
and you said you'd also like to share it here on Office Ladies.

5
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:19.090
Yes.

6
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:27.090
And this is our second try at this because I got so emotional the first time we started

7
00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.030
talking about it.

8
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:33.410
It's just really hard when someone you care about is going through so much.

9
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:37.950
But I told Angela that if she starts crying, then I'll start crying.

10
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:38.530
Yeah.

11
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.630
I know, Jenna, you have so much you want to say.

12
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:42.870
Yeah.

13
00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:48.970
So I'm aware that this is a big share, and it's kind of hard to know where to start.

14
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:54.750
But since I'm one of those people who tends to deal with emotional subjects by leaning into facts and

15
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.650
statistics, we all know that an Excel spreadsheet is my happy place.

16
00:00:58.730 --> 00:00:59.550
It really is.

17
00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:00.710
I will start there.

18
00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:07.630
Last December, I was diagnosed with stage one triple positive breast cancer.

19
00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:12.350
And for anyone who doesn't know what that means, I did not have a clue.

20
00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:18.870
Triple positive breast cancer is a very aggressive form of breast cancer that can spread and grow

21
00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:19.610
quite quickly.

22
00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.830
But luckily, my cancer was caught very early.

23
00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.630
It had not spread into my lymph nodes or

24
00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:26.830
anywhere else in my body.

25
00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:30.970
However, it still required the greatest hits of cancer treatments,

26
00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.090
surgery, chemotherapy, radiation.

27
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:38.450
All of which has been going on this past year.

28
00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.530
And lady, I know someday you're going to share more

29
00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:45.630
about this in your time when you're ready.

30
00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:49.990
But I just have to tell everyone, as your BFF,

31
00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:53.610
I can't believe how much you held on to these past few months.

32
00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:58.510
Well, I have to say, I've had a lot of people helping me hold on to this.

33
00:01:58.670 --> 00:01:59.050
I know.

34
00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.290
I did not carry this alone.

35
00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:06.130
I know you didn't, but you just had such courage and such grace.

36
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.570
And, you know, I'll cry if we talk

37
00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:10.290
about it too much.

38
00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:15.190
But I want you to share the first steps after you were diagnosed.

39
00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:16.490
Yes.

40
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:21.550
So the first thing was I had surgery in January.

41
00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.610
Then I did 12 rounds of chemotherapy.

42
00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.050
I had to do it every week.

43
00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.950
I completed that in May.

44
00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.690
And then I completed three weeks of radiation

45
00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:33.670
in July.

46
00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:41.090
And I like sharing those details, Angela, because those were things when I was diagnosed,

47
00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:46.170
when I was reading about other people's stories, I appreciated those details.

48
00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.250
So that's why I'm

49
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.230
offering them now.

50
00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:52.190
I also want to say that I was recently re-screened.

51
00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.570
I can very happily say that

52
00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.610
I am cancer-free.

53
00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:56.810
Cancer-free.

54
00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:57.510
Yes.

55
00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:57.630
Yes.

56
00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.510
I remember the day you told me that you were cancer-free.

57
00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.410
I remember how emotional we were

58
00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.090
in that moment.

59
00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:05.090
It was tears.

60
00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.810
And we were so thankful to hear those words.

61
00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:09.610
How does it feel

62
00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.210
for you to finally share this?

63
00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:15.150
Well, it all still feels very surreal.

64
00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:19.250
Even as I'm saying this out loud, even after making this

65
00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.210
announcement, even after living through it, I can't believe it's true.

66
00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.350
I mean, it's just,

67
00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:27.010
it's one of those things that you just never think is going to happen to you.

68
00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:27.370
Yeah.

69
00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:31.390
I mean, for a long time after the diagnosis came down, Lee and I just kept thinking that

70
00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.350
this was some mistake on the paperwork.

71
00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:33.830
Yeah.

72
00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:36.890
I remember just saying to you, like, are they sure?

73
00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:37.910
Yeah.

74
00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.630
And, you know, I am still receiving treatments.

75
00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.650
There are things that are designed

76
00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:44.770
to keep me cancer-free.

77
00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:49.470
So I get an infusion every three weeks of a drug that's called Herceptin.

78
00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:54.610
I'm also taking a drug each day to block my body from absorbing estrogen.

79
00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.370
So I'm still

80
00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:00.770
riding waves of super fun, random side effects.

81
00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:04.650
But I am over the hump of the big treatments and

82
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.170
I'm feeling more hearty.

83
00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:10.710
And I really wanted to share my story in case it can help other women.

84
00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.530
Really, that's what it's about for me.

85
00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:12.810
Yeah.

86
00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:12.860
Yeah.

87
00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:18.530
We talked a lot about how you wanted to go through your treatment with privacy and how

88
00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:19.330
important it was.

89
00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:24.890
All I could think about during this time, Jenna, was that I just wanted to protect

90
00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.170
you, you know?

91
00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:31.370
And I wanted you to be able to focus all of your energy on your treatment and healing.

92
00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:35.990
And I knew that when you were ready that there would be a time for sharing.

93
00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:37.570
And I also know that

94
00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:40.130
you sharing is going to help so many people.

95
00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.270
And now you're ready to share.

96
00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:43.210
Yeah.

97
00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:45.510
I mean, I did need that bubble.

98
00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:46.270
Yeah.

99
00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:50.450
I did need to focus all my energy on my treatment and my family.

100
00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:51.150
Of course.

101
00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:51.770
I have kids.

102
00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.010
You have young kids.

103
00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:58.690
And this was really that time where you just needed the space to heal.

104
00:04:59.010 --> 00:04:59.250
Yes.

105
00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:04.850
And to put your health first, do you want to tell everyone how you found out?

106
00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:05.790
Yeah.

107
00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:10.370
I also want to say, Angela, you are a great protector.

108
00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.410
I lost my hair during chemotherapy

109
00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:19.190
and I was wearing these hats with fake hair coming out the back to all of our podcast recordings,

110
00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:20.330
all of our meetings.

111
00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:25.630
You guys, Angela started wearing hats to all our meetings, too.

112
00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:26.570
We became

113
00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:27.370
the hat gals.

114
00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:30.050
And it was really moving to me, Angela.

115
00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.550
This was your idea.

116
00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.230
Angela also came over

117
00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:39.670
to my house and she stayed with my kids during my surgery so that they didn't have to go to school

118
00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:40.230
that day.

119
00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:43.570
And it just meant so much to me that they were with you.

120
00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:44.370
Well.

121
00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:49.710
Well, I could go on and on about all the ways that Angela and Josh supported us during this time.

122
00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:56.450
But to answer your question about how I found out, it was through my routine mammogram.

123
00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:02.470
And by the way, that test was inconclusive because I have really dense breast tissue.

124
00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:07.690
So my doctor ordered a follow-up ultrasound and that is when they found the tumor.

125
00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:12.670
It was in my left breaSt. It was too small to feel on a physical exam.

126
00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:21.450
So I don't know exactly how my sharing can be of service, but maybe this is your reminder out there

127
00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:28.410
to schedule your mammogram because it was that routine appointment that caught my cancer early

128
00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:32.930
enough that it had not spread and it was more easily treatable.

129
00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:34.930
It's so important.

130
00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:39.590
It's something you and I have talked about a lot that, you know,

131
00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:44.370
it's easy to put those things off and to put yourself second.

132
00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:45.950
You take care of everyone else.

133
00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:47.010
You put yourself second.

134
00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:53.690
And I remember after you were diagnosed that you, you know, I was just amazed

135
00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:59.410
by you, Jenna, because you just did that thing that you always do, which is you immediately wanted to get

136
00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.390
as much information as possible.

137
00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:02.890
Yeah.

138
00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.710
I mean, I was scared.

139
00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:08.710
And the thing that made me feel better

140
00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.490
was that information gathering.

141
00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:14.270
I really scoured the internet looking for any information I could

142
00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:15.650
find about my diagnosis.

143
00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:20.330
I read interviews and cancer blogs and Reddit threads.

144
00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.330
I got connected with

145
00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.270
an amazing team of doctors and nurses.

146
00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:29.410
They have been so patient and explained things over and over

147
00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:31.910
again until I understand them.

148
00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:35.210
Their patience is amazing.

149
00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:38.410
And then I got connected to other women

150
00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:41.770
who had had breast cancer and they helped me.

151
00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:44.110
And I really want to pay that forward.

152
00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:47.170
So, um, this is just the start.

153
00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:51.210
I hope to share more about my journey in the future, but right now,

154
00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.730
lady, we have a rewatch to finish.

155
00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:58.770
We do because I love doing our podcaSt. I love it so much.

156
00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:04.010
And I want to say thank you to you and to Sam and Cassie.

157
00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:07.150
I just think that the space that we have

158
00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:13.870
