1526
01:07:32.170 --> 01:07:40.690
Like, how is Jim not noticing that I've turned into a complete sad sack and I'm just standing there like a big, wet blanket?

1527
01:07:41.050 --> 01:07:43.110
I mean, how about some subtlety, Jenna?

1528
01:07:43.750 --> 01:07:48.430
When Jenna says a Razzie award, she's talking about a thing called the Golden Raspberry Awards.

1529
01:07:48.670 --> 01:07:52.890
It's a parody and it's an award show honoring the worst in cinematic failures.

1530
01:07:52.890 --> 01:07:53.710
Yes.

1531
01:07:54.030 --> 01:07:59.110
They don't even cover television, but I think they should make an exception for me in this scene.

1532
01:07:59.190 --> 01:07:59.240
Stop it.

1533
01:07:59.430 --> 01:08:00.190
I disagree.

1534
01:08:00.670 --> 01:08:00.950
Ugh.

1535
01:08:01.270 --> 01:08:13.270
Well, anyway, as if you couldn't tell, Pam is now very preoccupied with this idea that Daryl has planted in her head that maybe Jim is not actually as happy as he seeMs.

1536
01:08:13.270 --> 01:08:19.130
Yeah, Jim is going to present Dwight with a crown that he's made out of, like, tinfoil and cardboard.

1537
01:08:19.510 --> 01:08:20.870
Everyone applauds but Pam.

1538
01:08:21.010 --> 01:08:22.410
In fact, she runs outside.

1539
01:08:22.710 --> 01:08:23.790
Very dramatically.

1540
01:08:24.110 --> 01:08:25.030
Runs away.

1541
01:08:26.250 --> 01:08:27.750
Overly dramatic, Pam.

1542
01:08:28.430 --> 01:08:32.470
Dave said that Rain improvised a line at the end of this scene.

1543
01:08:32.850 --> 01:08:35.990
Originally, it was going to end with Pam running out.

1544
01:08:36.550 --> 01:08:39.510
But Rain improvised this line and I loved it so much.

1545
01:08:39.770 --> 01:08:44.450
He says, from now on, anyone who needs to speak to me has got to go through me firSt.

1546
01:08:44.870 --> 01:08:46.750
I thought it was really funny.

1547
01:08:48.010 --> 01:08:50.090
Rain knew his character so well.

1548
01:08:50.250 --> 01:08:50.690
So well.

1549
01:08:50.990 --> 01:08:53.290
Well, Jim is going to catch up to Pam outside.

1550
01:08:53.290 --> 01:08:55.410
They're in that little alley by the warehouse.

1551
01:08:55.890 --> 01:08:56.970
And she's worried.

1552
01:08:57.110 --> 01:08:58.010
Jim's like, are you okay?

1553
01:08:58.010 --> 01:08:59.530
And she says, today was fun.

1554
01:08:59.610 --> 01:09:00.710
But what about a year from now?

1555
01:09:00.810 --> 01:09:02.310
What about five years from now?

1556
01:09:02.310 --> 01:09:07.770
You know, she's worried that she's not enough for him and that he's going to resent her.

1557
01:09:08.070 --> 01:09:09.430
I need to pick up my mug.

1558
01:09:09.590 --> 01:09:09.930
Okay.

1559
01:09:10.210 --> 01:09:11.070
Here it comes.

1560
01:09:11.190 --> 01:09:11.870
Pockets mug.

1561
01:09:12.270 --> 01:09:12.710
All right.

1562
01:09:13.430 --> 01:09:15.450
This is when Pam lost me.

1563
01:09:15.810 --> 01:09:16.230
Uh-oh.

1564
01:09:16.330 --> 01:09:16.630
Okay.

1565
01:09:16.870 --> 01:09:18.050
I'm going to eat my granola bar.

1566
01:09:18.150 --> 01:09:18.290
Go.

1567
01:09:18.890 --> 01:09:23.710
For most of the season, Jim has been on my s*** liSt.

1568
01:09:24.470 --> 01:09:28.050
But all of this is very crazy making to me on Pam's part.

1569
01:09:28.230 --> 01:09:28.550
Hold up.

1570
01:09:28.610 --> 01:09:30.070
Are you calling bulls*** on Pam?

1571
01:09:30.310 --> 01:09:31.750
Are you playing a bulls*** card?

1572
01:09:31.750 --> 01:09:37.130
I don't know if it's a full bulls*** card because this is in character for them.

1573
01:09:37.750 --> 01:09:42.030
This is just where their relationship is making me a little crazy.

1574
01:09:42.530 --> 01:09:44.310
But herein lies the problem.

1575
01:09:44.650 --> 01:09:50.050
In this scene, Jim says, this was my decision to come back.

1576
01:09:50.130 --> 01:09:50.410
Okay?

1577
01:09:50.570 --> 01:09:51.670
I'm not going to resent you.

1578
01:09:51.770 --> 01:09:52.870
This was my decision.

1579
01:09:53.430 --> 01:09:55.010
That's everything you need to know.

1580
01:09:55.190 --> 01:09:56.230
This is their problem.

1581
01:09:56.450 --> 01:09:58.310
He decided to start the business.

1582
01:09:58.310 --> 01:10:00.910
And now he's decided to give up the business.

1583
01:10:00.910 --> 01:10:03.430
Why are they not making decisions together?

1584
01:10:03.430 --> 01:10:04.970
And I am losing my mind.

1585
01:10:05.150 --> 01:10:06.430
He bought a house.

1586
01:10:06.730 --> 01:10:07.290
Yes.

1587
01:10:07.590 --> 01:10:12.810
I remember hearing this amazing advice very early on about decision making in marriage.

1588
01:10:12.970 --> 01:10:14.970
And this is what I want to say to Jim and Pam.

1589
01:10:14.970 --> 01:10:20.510
When you're at odds over something, but you reach a compromise or you do eventually make

1590
01:10:20.510 --> 01:10:26.730
a decision, that decision is not complete until you both agree to take responsibility for

1591
01:10:26.730 --> 01:10:27.310
the decision.

1592
01:10:27.850 --> 01:10:32.610
So later on, if something goes wrong, you can't be like, see, I knew it.

1593
01:10:32.710 --> 01:10:33.970
Or like, well, that was you.

1594
01:10:34.110 --> 01:10:35.210
You're the one who wanted it.

1595
01:10:35.210 --> 01:10:36.530
Yeah, no, I told you so.

1596
01:10:36.670 --> 01:10:37.290
None of that.

1597
01:10:37.590 --> 01:10:40.130
Whatever the consequences, we both made it.

1598
01:10:40.290 --> 01:10:46.810
And if Jim and Pam had made the decision together to start this business and they took mutual

1599
01:10:46.810 --> 01:10:51.410
responsibility for how that decision played out, we'd be in a very different situation

1600
01:10:51.410 --> 01:10:51.950
right now.

1601
01:10:52.230 --> 01:10:57.550
If Pam was unhappy with that decision, too bad because you made that decision together.

1602
01:10:57.790 --> 01:10:59.450
You're going to have to tough it out, Pam.

1603
01:10:59.710 --> 01:11:01.030
That was a mutual decision.

1604
01:11:01.310 --> 01:11:03.950
These are the consequences of your mutual decision.

1605
01:11:04.630 --> 01:11:07.370
But all that happens is Jim makes decisions.

1606
01:11:08.170 --> 01:11:11.850
But Pam is like letting this happen, too.

1607
01:11:12.030 --> 01:11:12.710
You know what I mean?

1608
01:11:12.830 --> 01:11:14.250
Like, she just sort of like.

1609
01:11:14.430 --> 01:11:15.830
Well, she's got to be more vocal.

1610
01:11:16.030 --> 01:11:16.330
Yes.

1611
01:11:16.330 --> 01:11:18.630
And he's got to stop making decisions without her.

1612
01:11:18.970 --> 01:11:19.350
Yes.

1613
01:11:19.570 --> 01:11:20.130
Thank you.

1614
01:11:20.350 --> 01:11:21.030
Mug down.

1615
01:11:21.250 --> 01:11:22.410
Thank you for hearing me.

1616
01:11:23.010 --> 01:11:24.410
Well, Jim is going to have a talking head now.

1617
01:11:24.530 --> 01:11:25.750
He's going to say not enough.

1618
01:11:26.190 --> 01:11:30.470
And then he looks at the documentary crew and he said, look, I need to ask a favor from

1619
01:11:30.470 --> 01:11:30.870
you guys.

1620
01:11:31.010 --> 01:11:32.390
I know it's probably against the rules.

1621
01:11:32.910 --> 01:11:36.750
And then we hear Dave Rogers voice say, OK, you got it, man.

1622
01:11:37.110 --> 01:11:39.370
Very quick to say yes, I have to say.

1623
01:11:39.490 --> 01:11:39.770
I know.

1624
01:11:40.010 --> 01:11:43.330
I thought maybe they'd be like, let me think about it.

1625
01:11:43.390 --> 01:11:44.510
Let me talk to some people.

1626
01:11:44.530 --> 01:11:46.910
Or maybe just don't have them respond at all.

1627
01:11:47.230 --> 01:11:49.170
I didn't think we needed the response.

1628
01:11:49.350 --> 01:11:49.850
I didn't either.

1629
01:11:50.010 --> 01:11:51.570
It sort of like threw me for a second.

1630
