01:14:38.390 --> 01:14:40.570
And they even eat the same kind of paper.

1702
01:14:40.930 --> 01:14:41.330
Mm-hmm.

1703
01:14:41.570 --> 01:14:41.950
Mm-hmm.

1704
01:14:42.750 --> 01:14:46.950
Well, we had to ask Dave Rogers about the scene because a while back he shared with us

1705
01:14:46.950 --> 01:14:48.810
his love of Battlestar Galactica.

1706
01:14:48.930 --> 01:14:51.130
And how it influenced the character of Dwight.

1707
01:14:51.270 --> 01:14:52.250
Here's what he told us.

1708
01:14:52.430 --> 01:14:57.050
For this episode, it was scripted that Dwight paints and hangs a model of the Battlestar

1709
01:14:57.050 --> 01:14:58.190
Galactica in his office.

1710
01:14:58.790 --> 01:15:04.150
And just to go back in history for a second, when Dave met Greg Daniels after watching the

1711
01:15:04.150 --> 01:15:10.210
pilot, he pitched that Dwight should like Battlestar Galactica and have a Viper, one of the individual

1712
01:15:10.210 --> 01:15:11.950
fighter ships, on his desk.

1713
01:15:12.170 --> 01:15:12.530
Yes.

1714
01:15:12.730 --> 01:15:17.210
Dave talked about this in his interview with us, that originally Dwight was going to love

1715
01:15:17.210 --> 01:15:19.350
Star Trek, which he does love Star Trek.

1716
01:15:19.530 --> 01:15:25.670
But Dave pitched that it would be cooler if he liked this kind of niche sci-fi thing.

1717
01:15:25.830 --> 01:15:28.770
And that is why Dwight came to love Battlestar Galactica.

1718
01:15:28.770 --> 01:15:29.530
Yes.

1719
01:15:29.770 --> 01:15:35.870
Dave said Greg even bought him a model of the original Galactica Cylon base ship for one

1720
01:15:35.870 --> 01:15:36.630
of his birthdays.

1721
01:15:37.430 --> 01:15:41.750
And when they were prepping this episode, Phil Shea asked if Dwight would have an original

1722
01:15:41.750 --> 01:15:44.250
series Galactica or the new series Galactica.

1723
01:15:44.430 --> 01:15:47.910
He loves both series, but he wanted the original Galactica.

1724
01:15:47.910 --> 01:15:52.670
And when the show wrapped filming, Phil Shea said that he could keep it and gave it to him.

1725
01:15:52.890 --> 01:15:56.470
And Rain signed it and wrote, Dave Galactica loves you.

1726
01:15:56.590 --> 01:15:59.290
And he has it to this day displayed in his office.

1727
01:15:59.510 --> 01:16:01.910
And we saw it when we did our interview with him.

1728
01:16:02.030 --> 01:16:04.110
We could see it hanging in the background.

1729
01:16:05.130 --> 01:16:08.750
Well, I was wondering if we had to get special permission to use the ship.

1730
01:16:08.890 --> 01:16:11.490
But Steve Burgess said, legal said, use it.

1731
01:16:11.690 --> 01:16:12.270
Just use it.

1732
01:16:12.490 --> 01:16:12.910
Oh.

1733
01:16:13.330 --> 01:16:17.290
He said that we were not using it in any way that it was not intended.

1734
01:16:17.650 --> 01:16:20.490
Like it was a model that you paint and hang.

1735
01:16:20.610 --> 01:16:21.950
And that's what we did with it.

1736
01:16:22.270 --> 01:16:23.390
So it was OK.

1737
01:16:23.490 --> 01:16:26.110
And also, we weren't saying anything bad about it.

1738
01:16:26.250 --> 01:16:28.290
And also, it's a universal show.

1739
01:16:28.670 --> 01:16:28.910
OK.

1740
01:16:29.630 --> 01:16:31.450
Well, Dwight shows Esther out the door.

1741
01:16:31.650 --> 01:16:36.730
He gets a beanbag that says now on it and throws it at the back of Jim.

1742
01:16:36.890 --> 01:16:37.710
The summoning bag.

1743
01:16:37.910 --> 01:16:39.310
Yes, it's a summoning bag.

1744
01:16:39.390 --> 01:16:42.950
And he tells Jim he's going to need him to perform a test on a baby.

1745
